.60.10.0/24) and lan-b (node3, eth2, 10.60.20.0/24): added static interface addresses on node1's eth1/eth2, persistent ens7 addresses+routes on node2/node3 (Ubuntu 16.04, via /etc/network/interfaces.d), and a VyOS ipv4 forward filter with rule 5 (accept established/related), rule 10 (accept TCP/5432 from eth1->eth2 only), rule 900 (reject all else), default-action drop. Verified node2->node3:5432 succeeds while ping and other TCP ports are rejected. Completed the mandatory restart protocol on all three nodes sequentially (node1 router first, then node2, then node3), confirming changed boot_id on each and re-verifying the firewall policy and config persistence after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected topology: node1=VyOS with eth0(mgmt)/eth1/eth2, node2/node3=Ubuntu 16.04 with ens2(mgmt)/ens7\",\"Determined eth1<->node2 and eth2<->node3 mapping via ping test on trial addressing\",\"Configured node1 eth1=10.60.10.1/24, eth2=10.60.20.1/24 via VyOS configure/commit/save\",\"Configured persistent ens7 addresses on node2 (10.60.10.2/24) and node3 (10.60.20.2/24) via /etc/network/interfaces.d, with 'up ip route' directives for cross-lan routes via node1\",\"Verified ip_forward and per-interface forwarding already enabled on VyOS\",\"Configured VyOS firewall ipv4 forward filter: rule 5 accept established/related, rule 10 accept tcp dport 5432 eth1->eth2, rule 900 reject all, default-action drop; committed and saved\",\"Tested with nc listener on node3:5432 - confirmed TCP/5432 from node2 succeeds and payload received; confirmed ping and TCP/22 both directions rejected\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline on all 3 nodes\",\"Restarted node1 via 'sudo reboot' (backgrounded so ack returned first), polled until exec available, confirmed new boot_id, re-verified firewall rules/interfaces persisted, re-tested TCP 5432 allow / port22+ping reject\",\"Restarted node2, polled until available, confirmed new boot_id, verified ens7 IP/route persisted, re-tested policy\",\"Restarted node3, polled until available, confirmed new boot_id, verified ens7 IP/route persisted, ran final end-to-end test and checked VyOS rule hit counters incremented across all tests\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Allow node2->node3 TCP/5432\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9cdce5d036264d76\",\"cmd-62a553731d54444f\",\"cmd-1205f68d12494673\",\"cmd-b97f2d2439684ab5\"],\"summary\":\"nc listener on node3:5432 received 'hello' payload sent from node2; VyOS rule 10 counter incremented to 1 packet\"},{\"requirement\":\"Reject all other traffic between lan-a and lan-b (baseline)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2565ea27ec0a458f\",\"cmd-3f07a1aabcf44a27\",\"cmd-05f5eb23917b45a2\",\"cmd-b97f2d2439684ab5\"],\"summary\":\"ping and TCP/22 from node2->node3 and node3->node2 both rejected (ICMP port-unreachable / TCP connection-refused); VyOS rule 900 counter incremented to 4\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a02e6ae38ade49d3\",\"cmd-4586d57d83664189\",\"cmd-3361235a23fc413e\",\"cmd-c20d1c25d7e84b3a\"],\"summary\":\"Captured node1 interfaces, VyOS identity, boot_id 7668189d..., and committed firewall/interfaces config prior to restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9ebd3a0a8a2a4b26\",\"cmd-1a8e72f524c14977\",\"cmd-c4e9106aeaf94400\",\"cmd-9a8e3ece441c4e70\",\"cmd-53c84a227d1b436c\",\"cmd-6f815f255d4e4d46\",\"cmd-4a5be7350db24dd5\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sudo reboot' acked immediately; subsequent execs timed out/reset while rebooting; node1 became reachable again with boot_id a0df7da9... (changed from 7668189d...)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 recovered state (firewall/routing) after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7a5eef2ba51147f5\",\"cmd-f460884cb32d4601\",\"cmd-9f12e7d871ea4c98\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart: firewall ruleset (rules 5/10/900, default drop) and eth1/eth2 addresses intact; TCP/5432 allowed, TCP/22 rejected confirming policy still enforced